     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "plt.imshow(spatial_kernel(D,100))\n",
    "plt.colorbar()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "MlwJYzwMDkRH"
   },
   "source": [
    "Note that we're using Tensorflow maths operators inside our spatial kernel, since further on down we'll be using it inside Tensorflow-compiled code."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "AW1UnDrBCRGx"
   },
   "source": [
    "## Implementing the SEIR model in `gemlib`\n",
    "\n",
    "Having specified our _states_, the _transitions_ between states, and the rates at which they occur, we can start to assemble a model for the disease process.  We'll do this using `gemlib`'s `DiscreteTimeStateTransitionModel`, which embeds the above model into a discrete-time state transition stochastic process."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "Js2iaFYrJP9b"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Incidence matrix\n",
    "\n",
    "For the SEIR model we have 4 states `S, E, I, R` and 3 transitions `SE`, `EI` and `IR`. The incidence matrix is:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "yJ6kgJrfL-x_"
   },
   "source": [
    "````{exercise-start}\n",
    ":label: ex16.1\n",
    "````\n",
    "Set the incidence matrix for this model\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "vPfXKiFkMIFB",
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# incidence matrix"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "Jhn5znZIMK8E"
   },
   "source": [
    "````{solution-start} ex16.1\n",
    ":class: dropdown\n",
    "````"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "tHDMCf64-BwN",
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "incidence_matrix = np.array(\n",
    "    [ #  SE  EI  IR\n",
    "        [-1,  0,  0],  # S\n",
    "        [ 1, -1,  0],  # E\n",
    "        [ 0,  1, -1],  # I\n",
    "        [ 0,  0,  1],  # R\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    dtype=DTYPE\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "tLot2x0IESW6"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Initial state\n",
    "\n",
    "The initial state (or initial conditions) matrix describes the global state of the population at the start of the epidemic.\n",
    "\n",
    "We represent this as a `[N, M]` _one-hot_ encoding for $N$ individuals and $M$ states.  Here, the _one-hot_ encoding means that for each individual (i.e. row), there is at most one 1 indicating the state in which the individual exists.\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll start with individual id = 0 being infected, and everybody else susceptible."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "78O9yxovFEdu",
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "popsize = coords_df.shape[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "initial_state = np.concatenate(\n",
    "    [\n",
    "        np.repeat([[1, 0, 0, 0]], 99, axis=0),  # Susceptibles\n",
    "        [[0, 0, 1, 0]], # Initial infected\n",
    "        np.repeat([[1, 0, 0, 0]], 89, axis=0),\n",
    "        [[0, 0, 1, 0]],\n",
    "        np.repeat([[1, 0, 0, 0]], popsize-190, axis=0)\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    axis=0,\n",
    ").astype(DTYPE)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "/home/bridgen/Documents/git_repos/practical-epidemics/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/jax/_src/ops/scatter.py:108: FutureWarning: scatter inputs have incompatible types: cannot safely cast value from dtype=float64 to dtype=float32 with jax_numpy_dtype_promotion='standard'. In future JAX releases this will result in an error.\n",
      "  warnings.warn(\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "beta = 0.4\n",
    "alpha = 100.0\n",
    "sigma = 1/4.0\n",
    "gamma = 1/4.41\n",
    "epsilon = 3.8e-4\n",
    "h0 = 0.03\n",
    "\n",
    "K_mat = spatial_kernel(D, alpha)\n",
    "K = jnp.fill_diagonal(K_mat, jnp.zeros(K_mat.shape[0]), inplace=False)\n",
    "K0 = initial_state.shape[0] / jnp.sum(K)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "RLkcdRa6ARDj"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Transition rate functions\n",
    "\n",
    "Now we need to express our transition rates, which we do by creating a function for each transition.  which tuple of three arrays giving the transition rates between each state for each individual in the model.  Strict ordering of states and transition rates is maintained as for the incidence matrix above."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def se_rate(t, state): \n",
    "    return beta * jnp.matvec(\n",
    "    K0 * K, h0*state[:,1] + state[:,2]) + epsilon\n",
    "\n",
    "def ei_rate(t, state):\n",
    "    return sigma\n",
    "\n",
    "def ir_rate(t, state):\n",
    "    return gamma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "xlMgUSdrG_g1"
   },
   "source": [
    "We can check that our non-constant transition rate, SE, is returning something sensible if supplied the initial state:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "fJaxYy7hHFUU",
    "outputId": "d29869dd-ef19-4afa-d7d3-1a748fc88c68",
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "se transition rate shape:  (214,)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(\"se transition rate shape: \", se_rate(0.0, initial_state).shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "3eiTq0t0IIxo"
   },
   "source": [
    "which results in an array of length $N$ as expected."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "_lvHvq60F3Mo"
   },
   "source": [
    "### The discrete-time model"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "hY7PqPucNliR"
   },
   "source": [
    "````{exercise-start}\n",
    ":label: ex16.2\n",
    "````"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "9Kd06V38NnWH"
   },
   "source": [
    "Instantiate a `DiscreteTimeStateTransitionModel` using the components of the model defined above and run a simulation using the `sample` method and [0,0] as the random number seed. Use a time step of 1 (month) and 78 time steps. Plot the number of each type of transition happening in each month from the simulation output."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "vEzdJuHGMoNF"
   },
   "source": [
    "```\n",
    "seir = DiscreteTimeStateTransitionModel(\n",
    "    \n",
    ")\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "uhKRPhErNdsA"
   },
   "source": [
    "````{solution-start} ex16.2\n",
    ":class: dropdown\n",
    "````"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "lqt8GimZWRTD"
   },
   "source": [
    "Set up the model. Here, we supply a list of transition rate functions, ensuring the ordering matches the incidence matrix."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "kEjSEifGF2SY",
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "seir = DiscreteTimeStateTransitionModel(\n",
    "    transition_rate_fn=[se_rate, ei_rate, ir_rate],\n",
    "    incidence_matrix=incidence_matrix,\n",
    "    initial_state=initial_state,\n",
    "    initial_step=0,\n",
    "    time_delta=1.0,\n",
    "    num_steps=78\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "dmenOC9XNc_A"
   },
   "source": [
    "and run the simulation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "Hu0pnPUjMge0",
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "seir_sim = seir.sample(seed=jax.random.key(101))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 20,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "U155kmevHlxa",
    "outputId": "c8be65af-f7ca-4d0d-f45d-65d8aceeb1f1",
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
