  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "JKv8yZ1WPUlj"
   },
   "source": [
    "## Inference\n",
    "\n",
    "We now specify prior distributions for the model parameters.\n",
    "\n",
    "Let our epidemic model be written as\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "Z \\sim SIR(\\theta, \\mathbf{x}_0)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where $Z$ is the output transition events tensor (`seir_sim` above), $\\mathbf{x}_0$ is the initial state, and $\\theta = \\{\\beta,\\alpha,\\sigma,\\gamma,\\epsilon,h_0\\}$ are the parameters.  We pick priors for the parameters as follows:\n",
    "\n",
    "\\begin{align*}\n",
    "\\beta & \\sim Gamma(1,1) \\\\\n",
    "\\sigma & \\sim Gamma(2,8) \\\\\n",
    "\\gamma & \\sim Gamma(2,8) \\\\\n",
    "\\epsilon & \\sim Gamma(1,1) \\\\\n",
    "\\alpha & \\sim Gamma(1,1/50) \\\\\n",
    "h_0 & \\sim Beta(3,97)\n",
    "\\end{align*}\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "OPr95y-nkik3"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Implementing a Bayesian model"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "ox9PUMSgaG2G"
   },
   "source": [
    "````{exercise-start}\n",
    ":label: ex16.3\n",
    "````\n",
    "Set up the `JointDistributionCoroutine` for this model using the template code below and the definitions above."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "p_ZOZq5ZaS1y"
   },
   "source": [
    "```\n",
    "@tfd.JointDistributionCoroutine\n",
    "def model():\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Priors\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Epidemic model\n",
    "    incidence_matrix =\n",
    "\n",
    "    initial_state =\n",
    "\n",
    "    def transition_rates(t, state):\n",
    "\n",
    "    seir =\n",
    "    )\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "fnIymBaMaTk6"
   },
   "source": [
    "````{solution-start} ex16.3\n",
    ":class: dropdown\n",
    "````"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 27,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "MUVcIcN2fJwC",
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "@tfd.JointDistributionCoroutineAutoBatched\n",
    "def model():\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Priors\n",
    "    beta = yield tfd.Gamma(\n",
    "        concentration=DTYPE(1.0), rate=DTYPE(1.0), force_probs_to_zero_outside_support=True, name=\"beta\",\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    alpha = yield tfd.Gamma(\n",
    "        concentration=DTYPE(1.0), rate=DTYPE(1/50.0), force_probs_to_zero_outside_support=True, name=\"alpha\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    sigma = yield tfd.Gamma(\n",
    "        concentration=DTYPE(2.0), rate=DTYPE(8.0), force_probs_to_zero_outside_support=True, name=\"sigma\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    gamma = yield tfd.Gamma(\n",
    "        concentration=DTYPE(2.0), rate=DTYPE(8.0), force_probs_to_zero_outside_support=True, name=\"gamma\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    epsilon = yield tfd.Gamma(\n",
    "        concentration=DTYPE(1.0), rate=DTYPE(1.0), force_probs_to_zero_outside_support=True, name=\"epsilon\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    h0 = yield tfd.Beta(\n",
    "        concentration1=DTYPE(3.0), concentration0=DTYPE(97.0), force_probs_to_zero_outside_support=True, name=\"h0\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Epidemic model\n",
    "    incidence_matrix = np.array(\n",
    "        [ #  SE  EI  IR\n",
    "            [-1,  0,  0],  # S\n",
    "            [ 1, -1,  0],  # E\n",
    "            [ 0,  1, -1],  # I\n",
    "            [ 0,  0,  1],  # R\n",
    "        ],\n",
    "        dtype=DTYPE\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    initial_state = np.concatenate(\n",
    "        [\n",
    "            np.repeat([[1, 0, 0, 0]], 99, axis=0),  # Susceptibles\n",
    "            [[0, 0, 1, 0]], # Initial infected\n",
    "            np.repeat([[1, 0, 0, 0]], 89, axis=0),\n",
    "            [[0, 0, 1, 0]],\n",
    "            np.repeat([[1, 0, 0, 0]], popsize-190, axis=0)\n",
    "        ],\n",
    "        axis=0,\n",
    "    ).astype(DTYPE)\n",
    "\n",
    "    K_mat = spatial_kernel(D, alpha)\n",
    "    K = jnp.fill_diagonal(K_mat, jnp.zeros(K_mat.shape[0]), inplace=False)\n",
    "    K0 = initial_state.shape[0] / jnp.sum(K)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def se_rate(t, state): \n",
    "        return beta * jnp.matvec(K0 * K, h0*state[:,1] + state[:,2]) + epsilon\n",
    "\n",
    "    def ei_rate(t, state):\n",
    "        return sigma\n",
    "\n",
    "    def ir_rate(t, state):\n",
    "        return gamma    \n",
    "\n",
    "    yield DiscreteTimeStateTransitionModel(\n",
    "        transition_rate_fn=[se_rate, ei_rate, ir_rate],\n",
    "        incidence_matrix=incidence_matrix,\n",
    "        initial_state=initial_state,\n",
    "        initial_step=0,\n",
    "        time_delta=1.0,\n",
    "        num_steps=78,\n",
    "        name=\"seir\"\n",
    "    )"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "Nxvoi6-bjHs4"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Performing data-augmentation MCMC"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "AlN54K58jSYc"
   },
   "source": [
    "To make this example realistic, we're going to assume that the infection times are unobserved and try to infer them. In real life we might want to also try to infer many of the parameters of the model or at least the transmission parameters $(\\beta,\\alpha,\\epsilon)$, but here we're going to simplify the problem and just try to estimate $\\beta$ and $\\alpha$ (the transmission rate parameter and the spatial kernel scale parameter) alongside the infection times."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "yuBfPUf4j0Gp"
   },
   "source": [
    "We'll do this with a Metropolis-within-Gibbs algorithm, with an adaptive random walk step for updating the parameters and the `gemlib` implementation of the `move_events` algorithm for moving event times that we saw yesterday. `gemlib` provides a really neat interface for performing Metropolis-within-Gibbs algorithms, by chaining together MCMC kernels defined using the `MwgStep` method with the `>>` operator, to form compound kernels."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "0QNuGHHtpA1c"
   },
   "source": [
    "First we import the methods we need from the `gemlib.mcmc` module:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 28,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "oXnmCVOgT3GO",
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from gemlib.mcmc import adaptive_rwmh\n",
    "from gemlib.mcmc.discrete_time_state_transition_model import move_events\n",
    "from gemlib.mcmc import mcmc\n",
    "from gemlib.mcmc import multi_scan\n",
    "from gemlib.mcmc import MwgStep"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "SyNobMmOpK5Q"
   },
   "source": [
    "Then we define the kernels for the parameter updates and the infection time moves"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 29,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "kYGpy0SCXZJa",
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "param_mh_kernel = MwgStep(\n",
    "    sampling_algorithm = adaptive_rwmh(),\n",
    "    target_names=[\"beta\",\n",
    "                  \"alpha\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "se_move_kernel = MwgStep(\n",
    "    sampling_algorithm=move_events(\n",
    "        incidence_matrix=incidence_matrix,\n",
    "        transition_index=0,\n",
    "        num_units=1,\n",
    "        delta_max=5,\n",
    "        count_max=1,\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    target_names=[\"seir\"],\n",
    "    kernel_kwargs_fn=lambda _: {\"initial_conditions\": initial_state}\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "BzeegYoZpY4D"
   },
   "source": [
    "and chain them together, using the `multi_scan` method to say that we want to update the infection times for 10 individuals per each Metropolis-Hastings step for the parameters:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 30,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "6R8iBYzobAb5",
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "kernel =param_mh_kernel >> multi_scan(10, se_move_kernel)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "sI2w-DQSqQCO"
   },
   "source": [
    "We set the starting values for the parameters and event times in the chain (N.B. these values have been deliberately chosen to be close/equal to the true values)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
