  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "EcVxX3pes7RI"
   },
   "source": [
    "If we plot the trace plots for $\\beta$ and $\\alpha$ we can see that they don't look very satisfactory:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
     "height": 448
    },
    "id": "duGVbLCnXuGk",
    "outputId": "485a463c-3e70-4e7a-cd8a-b8260510a047",
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 2)\n",
    "ax[0].plot(samples.beta)\n",
    "ax[0].hlines(xmin=0, xmax=samples.beta.shape[0], y=0.4, color=\"red\")\n",
    "ax[1].plot(samples.alpha)\n",
    "ax[1].hlines(xmin=0, xmax=samples.beta.shape[0], y=100, color=\"red\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "a4jJycxrusDi"
   },
   "source": [
    "and this seems to be confirmed by calculating the acceptance rates for the parameter updates and infection time moves"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "KRGO9ykzpq3R",
    "outputId": "4976f90e-6470-45f9-acee-7ff1a92eda77"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "param_acc_rate = np.sum(info[0].is_accepted)/num_iterations\n",
    "param_acc_rate"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "Q3RMBy3PrEMk",
    "outputId": "d5e666e6-a44a-44ca-846b-89eb04d734be"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "se_move_acc_rate = np.sum(info[1][0].is_accepted)/(num_iterations)\n",
    "se_move_acc_rate"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "ocZAzdOLz6WC"
   },
   "source": [
    "We can visualise the mixing of the infection times by calculating the SE transition time for each individual for each iteration"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "_mUDh-_v0IwT"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# The output tensors for the seir object are of shape [K, T, N, L] for K MCMC\n",
    "# iterations, T timepoints, N individuals and L transitions.  We take a reverse\n",
    "# cumsum and a sum across the T dimension to get the time of the SE event for\n",
    "# each individual.\n",
    "se_time_samples = jnp.sum(jax.lax.cumsum(samples.seir, axis=-3, reverse=True), axis=-3)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "b-tVV8uj0vBD"
   },
   "source": [
    "and plotting it with `plt.imshow`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
     "height": 453
    },
    "id": "OsmFB2oLpGcZ",
    "outputId": "379bbfef-5e90-42bd-b943-943c6a7f4f7b"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plt.imshow(se_time_samples[:,:,0], aspect=\"auto\")\n",
    "plt.colorbar()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
